  "question": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/uyYQbA5EM9QoblBp8OwvSbG-U7lZkL3lIB7dJ0YQDpo.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>\nN equally spaced charges each of value q , are placed on a circle of radius R . The circle rotates about its axis with an angular velocity $\\omega$ as shown in the figure. A bigger Amperian loop B encloses the whole circle where as a smaller Amperian loop A encloses a small segment. The difference between enclosed currents, $I_A-I_B$, for the given Amperian loops is",
    "image": null
